-- S23 Maharashtra prose — astavinayak-circuit
-- Verdict matrix: 8 go / 2 skip / 2 wait
-- Anchors: 8-temple yatra ~620km, Sep 12-22 Ganesh Chaturthi 2026, Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4, Angarki dates, MTDC/MSRTC packages ₹3500-8000, traditional order Morgaon-Theur-Siddhatek-Ranjangaon-Ozar-Lenyadri-Mahad-Pali-return Morgaon

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('astavinayak-circuit', 1, 'go', 4, 'January runs the Ashtavinayak yatra at clean operational tempo. The full 620km circuit through eight Ganesha temples — five clustered in Pune district (Morgaon, Theur, Ranjangaon, Ozar, Lenyadri), two in Raigad (Mahad-Varadavinayak, Pali-Ballaleshwar), and one in Ahmednagar (Siddhatek on the Bhima river island) — closes cleanly in two intense days or three at standard pace with overnight at Pali or Mahad. Daytime 15-28C across the Pune plateau and Konkan side; Bhima river at navigable flow for the Siddhatek boat crossing; Konkan ghat roads to Pali clear of monsoon damage. MTDC and MSRTC packages run ₹3,500-5,500 per pilgrim for 2-night/3-day AC bus tours including all darshan timings, prasad meals, and budget lodging. Sankashti Chaturthi falls early month — the temples pick up Tuesday devotee flow without overwhelming queue density. Post-festival calm; the post-Ganesh-Chaturthi pilgrim residue from September has fully dispersed.', 'January at clean pradakshina temperature: 15-28C, Bhima river boat to Siddhatek operating, Konkan roads to Pali-Mahad fully open, MTDC bus packages ₹3,500-5,500. Two-day or three-day yatra both viable. Sankashti Chaturthi early month brings dignified Tuesday flow.', NULL),
('astavinayak-circuit', 2, 'go', 5, 'February is the secondary yatra peak. Maghi Ganesh Jayanti (Magh Shukla Chaturthi) falls Wednesday 4 February 2026 — the second-most-important Ashtavinayak observance of the year after Bhadrapada Ganesh Chaturthi. Morgaon and Theur run special pre-dawn abhishek rituals from 4am; all eight temples extend evening palki processions. Pre-festival pilgrim flow builds from late January and peaks Feb 3-5; the Tuesday before (Feb 3, also Angarki Chaturthi 2026) compounds the density. MTDC books out two weeks ahead through the festival window. Daytime 16-30C, nights 11-13C — among the most workable circuit weather of the year. Two-night/three-day operator packages run ₹4,000-6,000 with the festival surcharge. By mid-February the festival residue settles and the circuit returns to standard tempo through month-end. Best window for first-time pilgrims who want festival density without the September overload.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Wed Feb 4 + Angarki Chaturthi Tue Feb 3 — the second yatra peak. All eight temples on extended ritual schedule. Daytime 16-30C, perfect circuit weather. Book two weeks ahead through the festival window.', NULL),
('astavinayak-circuit', 3, 'go', 4, 'March holds the circuit at clean operational temperature through the first three weeks; the last week edges toward heat-stress territory. Gudi Padwa — the Marathi New Year — falls Thursday 19 March 2026; temples run special morning abhishek and the wider Maharashtra cultural anchor pulls pilgrim flow into the yatra circuit. Daytime 20-34C, nights 14-16C; the Pune plateau temples (Morgaon, Theur, Ranjangaon, Ozar, Lenyadri) hold mild noon temperatures while the Konkan side (Pali, Mahad) starts to feel the humidity build. Sankashti Chaturthi falls mid-March bringing standard Tuesday density. Bhima river at low pre-monsoon flow — Siddhatek boat crossing reliable. MTDC three-day packages ₹3,800-5,200. Lenyadri 307-step climb workable but pre-9am only; afternoon climbs sweat-heavy. Last clean-comfort window before April pushes the circuit into mid-day heat territory.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 — Marathi New Year cultural pull. Daytime 20-34C through first three weeks, humidity buildable but workable. Lenyadri 307 steps pre-9am only. Last clean window before April heat ramp.', NULL),
('astavinayak-circuit', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April pushes the Ashtavinayak yatra into heat-management territory. Daytime 26-39C across the Pune plateau; the Konkan side (Pali, Mahad) hits 32-36C with 70 percent humidity. The Pune-cluster temples (Morgaon, Theur, Ranjangaon, Ozar) remain workable as pre-9am and post-4pm darshans, but the in-between hours collapse — pradakshina pavements hit 50C surface temperatures by noon. Lenyadri 307-step climb impossible past 7am at 38C; only the half-loop (skip Lenyadri) circuit runs cleanly. Konkan ferry to Pali-Mahad route via Bhau-cha-Dhakka remains operational but the Konkan-side overnight halts struggle without AC. MTDC packages drop to ₹3,000-4,500 with the off-season cut; pilgrim arrivals thin sharply. Bhima river at lowest flow — Siddhatek boat crossing trivial but the island temple courtyard holds heat through evening. The yatra runs but at compressed pace.', 'April runs an attenuated yatra. Pre-9am and post-4pm darshans only. Lenyadri 307 steps impossible past 7am. Konkan-side humidity oppressive. MTDC rates drop 20 percent but the circuit experience compresses to early-morning fragments.', 'April pushes the Ashtavinayak circuit into heat-compromise territory. 26-39C Pune-side, 32-36C with 70 percent humidity Konkan-side. Pradakshina pavements 50C by noon. Lenyadri 307 steps impossible past 7am. Yatra runs but at fragmented pace; full-circuit experience collapses.'),
('astavinayak-circuit', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is the worst month of the year for the Ashtavinayak yatra. Daytime 30-42C across the Pune plateau; Konkan side 33-38C with 80 percent humidity (the pre-monsoon humidity ramp). Pradakshina pavements 55C noon surface; temple stone interiors hold heat through evening. Lenyadri 307-step climb unsafe at any time of day — the rocky north-facing approach holds direct sun 8am-5pm. Konkan ferry routes to Pali-Mahad still operational but the overnight halts at Pali-Mahad without AC are sleep-prohibitive. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 — the auspicious fast pulls dedicated pilgrims but only the Pune-cluster temples handle the volume; even committed pilgrims skip Lenyadri and the Konkan side. MTDC packages run ₹2,800-4,200 at deep off-season rates but the experience does not justify the saving. Push to October or November.', NULL, 'May is the unviable month. 30-42C Pune-side, 33-38C with 80 percent humidity Konkan-side. Lenyadri 307 steps unsafe all day. Pradakshina pavements 55C surface. The full eight-temple circuit cannot run cleanly. Push to October.'),
('astavinayak-circuit', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks the southwest monsoon arrival in Maharashtra. First-week rains break the heat — Pune plateau drops to 22-32C, Konkan side to 26-32C with daily rain. The landscape transforms; the Pune-cluster temples reset to their proper green-Maharashtra context. But the practical yatra runs into operational drag: Bhima river starts to swell, the Siddhatek island boat crossing becomes weather-dependent (the foot-bridge floods within days of heavy rainfall). Konkan-side roads to Pali-Mahad take 40 percent longer through ghat-section landslide caution. Lenyadri 307 steps rain-slippery — the rocky north-facing approach holds zero traction in wet weather. The circuit can still run if you accept day-of-yatra weather lottery; MTDC packages run ₹3,200-4,800 with the monsoon discount. Time it to the post-rain mornings when the temple landscapes look freshly washed; expect at least one wet darshan stretch across the three days.', 'June monsoon arrival breaks the heat — 22-32C Pune-side, lush green resets. But Bhima river swells (Siddhatek crossing weather-dependent), Konkan ghat roads slower, Lenyadri 307 steps rain-slippery. Yatra runs but with weather drag.', 'June runs as a transition month — landscape transformation but operational drag. Bhima river crossing to Siddhatek becomes day-of weather-dependent. Konkan ghats slower through landslide caution. Lenyadri 307 steps no-traction in wet weather.'),
('astavinayak-circuit', 7, 'skip', 2, 'July is the peak monsoon month — the full Ashtavinayak circuit collapses operationally. Konkan side hits 1500-2000mm rainfall through the month; Pali and Mahad-Raigad cut off from Pune by repeated ghat closures on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway and the Tamhini ghat approach. Bhima river floods through July — the Siddhatek island boat crossing suspends regularly; the foot-bridge submerges and the small fishing-boat backup runs only on weather windows. Karha river at Morgaon overflows the ghat steps; the temple platform stays workable but the approach floods. Kukdi river at Ozar runs high. Lenyadri 307 steps physically dangerous — rain-slick basalt holds zero grip. Sankashti Chaturthi falls in July (date varies by panchang) and a small dedicated pilgrim group still attempts the yatra; MTDC suspends the standard packages and only specialist religious operators run any service. Push to September festival window or October post-monsoon.', NULL, 'July monsoon peak — yatra collapses. Konkan ghat closures repeat through month; Bhima river floods Siddhatek island access; Lenyadri 307 steps physically dangerous in wet weather. MTDC suspends standard service. Push to September Ganesh Chaturthi window or October post-monsoon.'),
('astavinayak-circuit', 8, 'wait', 3, 'August holds the monsoon peak but adds the first major dedicated pilgrim pull of the year. Angarki Chaturthi — the Tuesday-Sankashti combination — falls Tuesday 4 August 2026, drawing committed pilgrim flow despite the rain. Konkan ghats remain unpredictable through month — Pali and Mahad reachable on dry-day windows only. Bhima river continues high; Siddhatek crossing suspends on heavy-rain days. The Pune-cluster temples (Morgaon, Theur, Ranjangaon, Ozar) run reliably — the temple stone holds; only the road approach gets wet. Lenyadri 307 steps remain hazardous. The MTDC standard bus packages start mid-month at reduced frequency; private operators run modified itineraries (Pune-cluster four-temple circuits, skipping Lenyadri, Siddhatek, Pali-Mahad). Pilgrim density picks up through final week as the Ganesh Chaturthi build approaches. Hotels at Theur and Ozar at full rate.', 'August opens with Angarki Chaturthi Aug 4 — committed pilgrims push through monsoon. Pune-cluster four-temple loop reliable; Lenyadri-Siddhatek-Pali-Mahad still weather-dependent. Pre-Ganesh-Chaturthi build through final week.', 'August holds the monsoon peak with operational uncertainty. Konkan ghats day-of-weather. Siddhatek crossing weather-dependent. The full eight-temple circuit cannot run reliably; only the Pune-cluster four-temple half-yatra closes cleanly.'),
('astavinayak-circuit', 9, 'go', 5, 'September is the absolute peak of the Ashtavinayak year. Ganesh Chaturthi (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. Every one of the eight Ashtavinayak temples runs continuous palki processions, dindi pilgrim groups arriving from across Maharashtra, special abhishek rituals every dawn, full puran-poli prasad distribution. Pune district sees its single largest annual pilgrim influx. MTDC, MSRTC, and private operator bus packages book out three months in advance; standard rates rise to ₹6,500-8,000 per pilgrim for the 3-day Ganesh-Chaturthi-window tour. Theur (Chintamani — the Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi temple) and Ranjangaon (Mahaganpati, with its 10-trunked 20-armed Maha Ganapati murti) draw the heaviest density. The full ten-day window operates at festival saturation; even the Konkan side (Pali, Mahad) handles the volume by extending darshan hours past midnight. Book 90 days ahead minimum.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sat Sep 12 to Anant Chaturdashi Tue Sep 22 — the absolute Ashtavinayak yatra peak. All eight temples on festival saturation. MTDC rates ₹6,500-8,000. Book 90 days ahead. Pune district largest annual pilgrim flow.', NULL),
('astavinayak-circuit', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is the post-monsoon ideal yatra window. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed but the residue density continues through the first two weeks; by mid-month the circuit settles into clean operational tempo at the freshest landscape of the year. Daytime 19-32C across the Pune plateau, Konkan side 22-32C — the green Maharashtra landscape at full post-rain saturation. Bhima river at navigable flow; Siddhatek boat crossing fully restored. Karha river at Morgaon at clean post-monsoon flow. Kukdi river at Ozar lush. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 — the auspicious mid-month pull brings dedicated pilgrim density without the September overload. MTDC three-day packages drop back to ₹4,500-6,000. Lenyadri 307-step climb at year-best traction — the freshly-washed basalt grips cleanly underfoot. Konkan ghats fully reopened. The circuit at its most photographable and most operationally clean.', 'Post-monsoon ideal. Lush green Maharashtra landscape, all rivers at clean flow, Konkan ghats reopened. Angarki Chaturthi Tue Oct 6 brings clean pilgrim density. MTDC ₹4,500-6,000. Lenyadri 307 steps at year-best traction.', NULL),
('astavinayak-circuit', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Ashtavinayak window. The post-monsoon green still holds through first two weeks; daytime 16-30C, nights 12-14C — the sharpest cool weather of the year suited to the long driving days the circuit demands. The full 620km loop closes cleanly in two intense days or three relaxed days. Bhima river at clean post-monsoon flow — Siddhatek crossing reliable. Konkan-side ghat roads to Pali-Mahad fully restored and at year-best surface condition. Pradakshina pavements cool underfoot. Lenyadri 307-step climb workable any time of day. Sankashti Chaturthi falls mid-month at standard density. MTDC three-day packages ₹4,000-5,500 — back to standard rates after the September surcharge cycle. Pune escape weekend traffic on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is the only operational caveat — book Saturday-Monday rather than Friday-Sunday to avoid the ghat-traffic bottleneck.', 'November year-best — 16-30C, post-monsoon green still holding, all rivers at clean flow, Konkan ghats restored. Lenyadri 307 steps any time of day. MTDC ₹4,000-5,500. Avoid Fri-Sun for the Pune escape weekend traffic.', NULL),
('astavinayak-circuit', 12, 'go', 4, 'December holds clean circuit weather with a Tuesday pilgrim anchor and the Pune escape tourist peak. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 1 December 2026 — the auspicious month-opener pulls dedicated pilgrim flow; the circuit runs at strong density through first week. Daytime 14-29C, nights 10-12C — the coolest stretch of the year, ideal for the long driving days; light woolens for the early-morning Lenyadri climb. Bhima river at full clean flow. Konkan ghats clear. MTDC three-day packages ₹4,200-5,800 at year-end tourist peak rates. The Mumbai-Pune Expressway runs heavy weekend traffic through the Pune-tourist-escape season; the circuit driving days take 15 percent longer through December weekends. Sri Ganesh festivals at the eight temples remain at standard tempo with Christmas-week visitor density layered on. Book mid-month weekdays for the cleanest operational experience; the last week (Dec 25-31) competes with Pune tourist holiday traffic for the same road infrastructure.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi opens the month strong. 14-29C, year-coolest stretch. MTDC ₹4,200-5,800. Mumbai-Pune Expressway heavy weekend traffic through Pune-tourist-escape season — book weekdays for cleanest experience.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
  why_go = EXCLUDED.why_go,
  why_not = EXCLUDED.why_not;
